      en: "Kulen Promtep Wildlife Sanctuary, established in 1993 in northern Cambodia, spans 3,750 km² of dry dipterocarp forest and savanna. It protects critically endangered species like the kouprey (Bos sauveli) and Asian elephant, and hosts over 300 bird species. The sanctuary is named after Phnom Kulen hill. Threats include illegal logging and poaching, mitigated by community patrolling and habitat restoration. It is part of the Eastern Plains Landscape and connects to other protected areas.",
